 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 518369,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Aidan decides to invest $3,200 annually in a mutual fund. He expects the fund to have a 10.8% interest rate compounded annually. How much will Aidan’s mutual fund account have after 15 years?",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>The future value is <span data-math=\"FV = pmt \\times \\frac{{{{\\left( {1 + \\frac{r}{n}} \\right)}^{n \\times t}} - 1}}{{\\frac{r}{n}}}\"></span>, where <i>FV</i> is the future value, <i>pmt</i> is the payment, <i>r</i> is the annual interest rate (in decimal form), <i>n</i> is the number of compounding periods per year, and <i>t</i> is the number of years. It is important to note that the number of deposits per year and the number of compounding periods per year must be the same.</p>\n<p>It will help you get the right answer using your calculator to find <span data-math=\"n \\times t\"></span> first.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"n \\times t = \\left( 1 \\right) \\times \\left( {15} \\right) = 15\"></span></p>\n<p><span data-math=\"FV = 3,200 \\times \\frac{{{{\\left( {1 + \\frac{{0.108}}{1}} \\right)}^{15}} - 1}}{{\\frac{{0.108}}{1}}}{\\text{  =  \\$108,352}}{\\text{.43}}\"></span></p>\n<p>The extra parentheses were added to help you enter the expression properly in your calculator.</p>\n"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "$108,352.43"
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  }
 ],
